**Information Collection and Use**

Most of what the app knows about you stays on your phone. The app does not ask you to create an account, does not ask for an email address or a password, and does not contain advertising, analytics or crash-reporting software.

Information kept on your device only, and never sent to me:

*   Your progress in each city: city coverage, best scores, your last 100 runs (a score and the time it was played), the questions you have already seen, and which city you played last.
*   A small counter that remembers whether you have been shown the "tap the map to drop a pin" hint.
*   A cached copy of the city data (street geometry and street-guide text) the app downloaded, so the game opens and plays without a network connection.

This information is removed when you uninstall the app or clear the app's data.

Information sent to the game server:

*   **A player name, only if you choose to sign in to the leaderboard.** Playing does not require it; all three game modes work without ever entering a name. The name is a name you invent, up to 13 characters. It is not protected by a password and it is shown publicly to other players on the leaderboard, so please do not use your full name, your email address, your phone number, or any other detail that identifies you personally.
*   **Your timed-run score for a city**, submitted together with that name so the leaderboard can rank it. Only the timed run is scored; the other two modes never send anything.
*   **A city name, only if you use the "request a city" link** to ask for a city the game does not yet cover. Only the city name you type is sent.
*   **Requests for game data** (the list of cities, and each city's streets and trivia). These carry no information about you beyond what any internet request carries.

**Log Data**

I want to inform you that whenever your app contacts the game server, the server records standard request information, called Log Data. This Log Data may include your device's Internet Protocol ("IP") address, the request that was made, the time and date of the request, and the software version making it. It is used to keep the service running and to diagnose failures, and it is not combined with your player name to build a profile of you.

The app itself contains no analytics or crash-reporting product; when something goes wrong it is written to the device's own console log and stays on your device.

**Permissions**

The app requests one permission: internet access, used to download city data and to read and write the leaderboard. It does not ask for and cannot access your location, your camera, your microphone, your contacts, your photos, or the files on your device. The map you play on is drawn from published municipal street registers, not from where you are.

